# Handheld Performance Budget

The game targets **60 FPS** on handheld hardware. Keep frame timing under control using these budgets:

| Phase | Budget |
|-------|--------|
| Render | **≤ 6.5 ms** |
| Fixed step (simulation / fixed timestep work) | **≤ 9.5 ms** |

Together these leave headroom for vsync, OS, and variance while staying within a 16.67 ms frame.

For optimization priorities, workflow, and tactics, follow **`docs/PERFORMANCE_OPTIMIZATION_STRATEGY.md`**.

**When performance falls short** (spikes, sustained misses, profiling showing over-budget work): **investigate root cause and address it** — do not ignore regressions or treat slowness as acceptable without analysis and a fix or an explicit, documented tradeoff in `docs/GAME_DESIGN.md` if behavior must change.

When touching hot paths (render loop, per-frame systems, navigation fields, collision, audio routing), prefer measuring (existing profiling logs, timers, frame stats) over guessing.
